NOTICE — Prior art and acknowledgements
=======================================

This project builds directly on the format research, reverse engineering, and
reference implementation published in:

    jwheare/mythextract
    https://github.com/jwheare/mythextract
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 James Wheare

mythextract is the source of our understanding of the Myth TFL and Myth II
monolith container layout, the TFL and SB tag header structures, the TFL-to-SB
tag header conversion, and the written format notes in its `docs/` directory.
Any code in this repository that is derived from or closely follows mythextract
remains subject to its MIT license, and is credited in place at the relevant
source files. NOTES.md documents what was taken from it, file by file.

mythextract is not vendored or redistributed here. It is cloned into a
git-ignored `reference/` directory for study only.

The mesh marker, marker-palette, and map-action structures in `src/mesh.py`
(and the map-action parameter type table specifically) were additionally
cross-checked against:

    Iron's Mesh Converter (Mac and Windows, with source)
    https://tain.totalcodex.net/items/show/mesh-converter-mac-and-windows-w-source-code
    "released as-is with permission from iron", uploaded 2011

No code from that tool is vendored or reproduced here; it was consulted only
as a second, independent source to validate struct layouts and the TFL/Myth II
parameter-type mapping already derived from mythextract, and the reasoning is
recorded in NOTES.md section 14.

The field descriptions in `src/fieldinfo.py` are short factual summaries, written
for this project, of behaviour documented in:

    Fear and Loathing documentation, v1.8.5
    Fear, Myth II, and content copyright 1998 Bungie Software
    Tyson (Ferrex) Green; distributed by Project Magma
    http://projectmagma.net

The manuals themselves are not reproduced or redistributed here. They were read
to learn what each mesh setting does and what values are usual, and that
knowledge is expressed in our own words with the manual credited at the point of
use. NOTES.md section 15 records what was learned, including the measurement
they made possible: that Myth II's terrain grid is genuinely double TFL's
resolution rather than a different bookkeeping convention.


